{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game","id":1117007,"title":"Cyanide's Werewolf: The Apocalypse video game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-16T16:32:52-07:00","id":1117007,"title":"Cyanide's Werewolf: The Apocalypse video game","content":"Some more information which is disappointing in some places and good elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E3-2017-Interview--Werewolf-The-Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://aggrogamer.com/assets/1484930318-8a9cb8b6a3ae7c13cf46a099da5b7a71.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E3-2017-Interview--Werewolf-The-Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\"> E3 2017 Interview &acirc;&euro;&rdquo; Werewolf: The Apocalypse </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E3-2017-Interview--Werewolf-The-Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\"> http://aggrogamer.com/article/5841/E3-2017-Interview--Werewolf-The-Apocalypse </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> At E3 I was able to sit down and gather more information on Werewolf: The Apocalypse from Julien Desourteaux. Here's what I was able to get on Werewolf: The Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> * You will be Ronin<br /> * You will be able to join different factions but that won't change the story<br /> * Pentex is the primary antagonist<br /> * A major theme is controlling your rage as you'll be able to kill friend and foe alike in frenzies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:34:22-07:00","id":1117051,"title":"","content":"Cutting Glabro and Hispo from the game probably merits a mention as a major thing to consider. It's a mixed one to me. On one hand, it's hard to imagine WtA without all five forms being a thing but I can see from a game-play perspective trying to find a role for all five could be tough (it's not like Forsaken where they did more to ensure that each form has a specific built in-situation they're best for).<br /> <br /> The Ronin vs. Pentex highly linear story seems like it's going to be an issue no matter how good the game play ends up. The Rage mechanics could be really good, but that doesn't seem like something to sell a whole video game on. The idea that they made sure to pull in dialog options as things that can stoke your Rage is good, but with a highly linear story Frenzies are either going to end the game, or the impact dies because no matter how many friends and innocents you kill, the plot will get pushed forward.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T20:00:46-07:00","id":1117065,"title":"","content":"Well, Pentex was always going to be the villain. Did people think they were going to use anything other than the iconic Garou antagonist?<br /> <br /> I think Frenzies and Rage getting so much focus isn't a good thing because I don't really care too much about that element. I don't want to really focus on being a psychopathic murder-hobo more in Werewolf than vampire.<br /> <br /> As for Linear Story, that may be overstated. After all, <b>Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines</b> has four endings but one single story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T20:43:10-07:00","id":1117072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117065#post1117065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Linear Story, that may be overstated. After all, <b>Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines</b> has four endings but one single story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And it's still so damn early, I'm sure things will change regardless, between now and the actual release.<br /> <br /> If it IS linear? That's cool, too. Redemption and Bloodlines were both very linear, and I had a blast playing each of them...<br /> <br /> hundreds of times.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T20:54:18-07:00","id":1117075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117065#post1117065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Pentex was always going to be the villain. Did people think they were going to use anything other than the iconic Garou antagonist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with the approach that ParaWolf has been taking, completely ignoring the &quot;shadowy and secretive&quot; part of Pentex and just hopping in and out into the open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T20:56:16-07:00","id":1117077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117075#post1117075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not with the approach that ParaWolf has been taking, completely ignoring the &quot;shadowy and secretive&quot; part of Pentex and just hopping in and out into the open.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's questionable even in the game world whether you can see the Pentex Logo and it's a fully legitimate holding company for all the other companies we know exist under it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:38:16-07:00","id":1117109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117065#post1117065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Pentex was always going to be the villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind that Pentex is the primary villain. I didn't say anything of the sort. I mean the specifics that we've heard in combination is a problem. Not that each individual element is a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Frenzies and Rage getting so much focus isn't a good thing because I don't really care too much about that element. </div> </div> </div>OK, but Rage is supposed to be a pretty present thing in WtA. The Curse and the Beast Within are hard to capture in a video game where the dialog is going to be largely be preset. It really comes down to how well you can manage Rage in the game. If it's like Humanity in Bloodlines, it's not such a big deal. Playing it so you're never at a bit risk means a more limited set of options you pick, where willing to drop a lot means you've got more options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Linear Story, that may be overstated. After all, <b>Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines</b> has four endings but one single story. </div> </div> </div>I don't mind linear stories in video games in general. But it's a problem if they present things that imply consequences of choice, because those choices don't end up having much effect. Bloodlines was very linear, but plenty of player choices matter. How you deal with the Gargoyle makes a difference towards your future relationship with the Tremere, even if it doesn't effect the endings. <br /> <br /> And again, the point is the combination. Something like the Rage mechanical ideas are lost on a highly linear game. It's not that linear games are bad, but that they're bad for specific mechanical elements to be added to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T05:09:06-07:00","id":1117151,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to talk about an ideal WtA game, you would have it set in a rural location. It would be near a state or national park (ideally the map would be 50% public land and 50% private land) and it would include a large town and a dozen or so small towns. A place like Aroostock County in Maine would be ideal, especially since there are a two Native American reservations in the county, so you have a good reason for Wendigo and Uktenu to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:05:37-07:00","id":1117165,"title":"","content":"Is it me, or are they heavily using the template of Bloodlines here? I mean, in general a ronin is not something that gets played often or mentioned often in WtA briefings. As for 'factions', let me guess Sactum of Gaia and such?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, might be good, I'm just kinda confused how heavily the garou vs humans angle is here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:47:30-07:00","id":1117177,"title":"","content":"Is it really a WtA game if you are playing a Ronin? I mean, Tribe is so central to the Garou experience that I do not really think that you can actually be Garou unless you have a Tribe (the Spirits of the Pact sure as heck do not think so). I would much rather have the character just choose a Tribe and run with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:24:42-07:00","id":1117303,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines is a classic of video games so following in its footsteps isn't a bad thing. It's also a Storyteller System game set in the same world so why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117177#post1117177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really a WtA game if you are playing a Ronin? I mean, Tribe is so central to the Garou experience that I do not really think that you can actually be Garou unless you have a Tribe (the Spirits of the Pact sure as heck do not think so). I would much rather have the character just choose a Tribe and run with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is yes.<br /> <br /> I've played many Ronin games.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I believe being a Ronin is for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. To explain why you don't have a pack.<br /> <br /> 2. To give you a chance to choose your own tribe after meeting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:39:39-07:00","id":1117320,"title":"","content":"Strange, I have never played in a game with a Ronin or known anyone to ever allow anyone to play a Ronin in nearly a quarter century of playing WtA. The fact that it is almost impossible get access to Caerns, Fetiches, Gifts, Kinfolk, Rites, Talons, etc means that it is very difficult to justify a Ronin in a campaign unless the ST really wants a Ronin in their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:50:48-07:00","id":1117336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117320#post1117320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange, I have never played in a game with a Ronin or known anyone to ever allow anyone to play a Ronin in nearly a quarter century of playing WtA. The fact that it is almost impossible get access to Caerns, Fetiches, Gifts, Kinfolk, Rites, Talons, etc means that it is very difficult to justify a Ronin in a campaign unless the ST really wants a Ronin in their game.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/51TAMRC2H9L._SX357_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> One of the best supplements of all time.<br /> <br /> Ronin are great characters because they're the mercenaries of the Garou Nation that have to live off the grid and make private backroom deals with packs and septs to take the worst jobs. You're an exile and a deniable asset in the complicated games of the Garou politics. It's a good premise for a single-player game as you never have to be caught up in pack or local politics but can go wherever the ST wants you. When you're a Ronin pack, though, you have a LOT more interesting potential missions too as suddenly you're a threat.<br /> <br /> It's also great for incorporating the greater WOD as Ronin can end up working for vampires, Pentex, Mages, and so on.<br /> <br /> Your goal isn't protecting Gaia, it's survival.<br /> <br /> Ronin games also have the benefit of allowing you to potentially have a more &quot;human&quot; view of the world like if you reject Gaian beliefs or want to just protect the local human population versus engage in a eternal war against Satan.<br /> <br /> The fact I often play Ronin games may be why I often forget the Skindancers are villains in my games since I've often used them in allied or friendly roles despite how intrinsically horrifying they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2017, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:19:56-07:00","id":1117400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117303#post1117303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines is a classic of video games so following in its footsteps isn't a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But from the sound of it they're not. Bloodlines is about a neonate thrust into the deep end of vampire politics and sect warfare. A Ronin is a werewolf that's already made a choice to not be part of the Garou Nation. Bloodlines lets you pick from all of the core 1e VtM Clans and select between the two initial Sects that 1e promoted as ones for players (the Anarchs and the Camarilla). Playing a Ronin means Tribes are out despite being one of the main character selection parts of WtA the whole run of the game. This is even more the case with the Unofficial Patch that adds lots more options to character creation.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines also has a lot of value in there being multiple ending mostly because there's not really one big bad. There's a plot to resolve in a fairly linear fashion, but depending on how you want to view it there's three potential final antagonists to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've played many Ronin games. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you're going to find yourself in a significant minority there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, I believe being a Ronin is for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. To explain why you don't have a pack.<br /> <br /> 2. To give you a chance to choose your own tribe after meeting them. </div> </div> </div>1) There's plenty of reasons to explain that without going full Ronin, and as you note, Ronin can still form packs.<br /> <br /> 2) It doesn't sound like you're going to be able to do that in the video game; just pick Tribes to ally with for perks. In TT play, you don't play Ronin to just a Tribe later, because Ronin rejected such things already. The few Tribes that would take a Ronin in later... you might as well just pick those Tribes to start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117336#post1117336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the best supplements of all time.</div> </div> </div> </div>...eh. It's not bad, but it's also contradicted a lot in other books. It's good for tweaking the game if these are the concepts you want to play, but it doesn't match well with how most of the character types are presented in the rest of the game lines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:51:36-07:00","id":1117501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117400#post1117400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from the sound of it they're not. Bloodlines is about a neonate thrust into the deep end of vampire politics and sect warfare. A Ronin is a werewolf that's already made a choice to not be part of the Garou Nation. Bloodlines lets you pick from all of the core 1e VtM Clans and select between the two initial Sects that 1e promoted as ones for players (the Anarchs and the Camarilla). Playing a Ronin means Tribes are out despite being one of the main character selection parts of WtA the whole run of the game. This is even more the case with the Unofficial Patch that adds lots more options to character creation.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines also has a lot of value in there being multiple ending mostly because there's not really one big bad. There's a plot to resolve in a fairly linear fashion, but depending on how you want to view it there's three potential final antagonists to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ronin don't normally make the choice to be part of Garou socitey. They're usually exiles and often for bullshit reasons. Take a look at the iconic Ronin in Albretch. He was exiled for no other reason than he pissed Jacob Morningkill off. The problem with that was that he found his own pack who took him in and thus lost all real problem with his exile. Personally, I think it's a better option because you can't play a Lost Cub unless you're very very young so being a Ronin is a much better option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure you're going to find yourself in a significant minority there. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but much like Thin Bloods in vampire, it's a missed opportunity not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) There's plenty of reasons to explain that without going full Ronin, and as you note, Ronin can still form packs. </div> </div> </div>WHich I hope you can do the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) It doesn't sound like you're going to be able to do that in the video game; just pick Tribes to ally with for perks. In TT play, you don't play Ronin to just a Tribe later, because Ronin rejected such things already. The few Tribes that would take a Ronin in later... you might as well just pick those Tribes to start. </div> </div> </div>Eh, they're avoiding making it a game where you have four people fighting alongside you (Thank Gaia) but you might be able to make a pack in the game. Just it won't get togther until the end of the game probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...eh. It's not bad, but it's also contradicted a lot in other books. It's good for tweaking the game if these are the concepts you want to play, but it doesn't match well with how most of the character types are presented in the rest of the game lines. </div> </div> </div>Such as?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:24:52-07:00","id":1117540,"title":"","content":"Being Ronin isn't something to celebrate, it's a short and brutal life at best and a shortcut to Wyrmish corruption at worst. You either do the worst jobs the Nation has to offer for the ability to learn Gifts or barter with spirits unscrupulous enough to teach you who could easily betray you to the Wyrm. You don't gain renown, have no sept to call home, and are highly isolated when your very nature cries out for companionship. If the game wants to focus on desperation it's a good choice but for anything else, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:39:10-07:00","id":1117544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117540#post1117540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Ronin isn't something to celebrate, it's a short and brutal life at best and a shortcut to Wyrmish corruption at worst. You either do the worst jobs the Nation has to offer for the ability to learn Gifts or barter with spirits unscrupulous enough to teach you who could easily betray you to the Wyrm. You don't gain renown, have no sept to call home, and are highly isolated when your very nature cries out for companionship. If the game wants to focus on desperation it's a good choice but for anything else, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's awesome.<br /> <br /> You're the cop...err Garou who doesn't play by the rules!<br /> <br /> Again, I think this will come off EXTREMELY like Bloodlines but Bloodlines is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2017, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:29:22-07:00","id":1117571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117501#post1117501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ronin don't normally make the choice to be part of Garou socitey.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books don't really portray this as the majority of Ronin being forced into it. It's generally discussed about evenly left or ostracized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take a look at the iconic Ronin in Albretch. </div> </div> </div>He was never a Ronin. He was exiled from his home Sept, and moved to a different one. He was never stripped of his Rank and Renown, and he was never ritually stripped of his Tribe. Treating ever political exile as a Ronin is not how the game operates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WHich I hope you can do the game. </div> </div> </div>Ronin packs (with the different names they've had over the years) aren't really going to add much besides having ally NPCs working with you given what else we know about the game. And, you know, the four people fighting alongside you thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such as? </div> </div> </div>W20, for example, makes zero mention of Ronin operating as mercenaries for the Garou Nation, and being like Shadowrunners with the Tribes being the megacorps. W20 presents the vast majority of Garou literally shunning Ronin completely and never stooping to doing anything with them besides chasing them off. It is a rare and usually small and desperate Sept that does such things, and they still charge the Ronin unfairly for access to their Caerns and any sort of help (like teaching Gifts).<br /> <br /> Basically, all the interesting stuff that Outcastes give them to do isn't acknowledged at all, because the default game doesn't consider Ronin to be things you play except for the possible redemption arc.<br /> <br /> Ronin aren't cops that don't have to play by the rules. They're cops that have left/were fired under such shameful circumstances that no respectable person would hire them, all the current cops hate them and punish them harsher if they don't follow the rules to the letter, every reporter would love to get a scoop on their further downfall, and the only people actively seeking to offer them a hand are the worst and most vile criminals in town.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> And that's where I don't see it following Bloodlines. In Bloodlines you're an illegal Embrace, but it's treated as being more like a Metis. Your sire is punished, but the Prince decides to spare you to use you as a tool. A Ronin gets booted out of the Protectorate instead of offered a job, with an apartment, and people helping out learn stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-17-2017, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:50:36-07:00","id":1117577,"title":"","content":"Eh, I hope they go the Outcast route.<br /> <br /> The depiction of Ronin in the game is something which I always felt was underdone outside of the aformeentioned book. Personally, I felt the Garou Nation should make regular use of exile as a way of dealing with people. However, ultimately, Outcasts does remain the best resource for dealing with Ronin and their culture. I also tend to think of Skinwalkers as one of the most severely unused elements of Garou society.<br /> <br /> Given you CAN join factions (and learn their gifts) I'm inclined to think it won't be the kind of &quot;Ronin&quot; which is treated as a shunned outcast but more a valuable asset that you remain apart of it.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; versus a outcast and that's the way it should be. Ronin are inherently cool after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:22:16-07:00","id":1117589,"title":"","content":"Why? Erebus is a much better solution if the Garou in question committed a grave crime and is willing to make amends. In my mind, most Ronin are cowards unwilling to pay for their crimes in Erebus rather than political exiles. They are no more cool than a deadbeat dad running from the law because he is unwilling to pay child support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:35:58-07:00","id":1117594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117589#post1117589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Erebus is a much better solution if the Garou in question committed a grave crime and is willing to make amends. In my mind, most Ronin are cowards unwilling to pay for their crimes in Erebus rather than political exiles. They are no more cool than a deadbeat dad running from the law because he is unwilling to pay child support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly you treat finding Erebus a different matter than in my games where it's about as easy as finding the Holy Grail and is semi-mythical.<br /> <br /> However, your view of Ronin is the view that there's anything to the Litany other than bullshit. A Garou who doesn't believe in hiding from humanity, who sincerely loves another Garou, or any number of awesome other stories is a great origin for Garou. I've mentioned in other threads I don't portray the Garou as &quot;good&quot; guys. No, they're a bunch of religious fundamentalists and very often grossly immoral controlled by politics as well as violence.<br /> <br /> A Ronin can very often be a person exiled for no damn good reason and who stands for their own beliefs. Say, a Garou who refuses to abandon his Homid religion.<br /> <br /> A Garou who needs his pack and tribe is probably understandable but the one who puts what is right above companionship is a figure who deserves respect.<br /> <br /> As for Albretch getting banished from his sept, The Silver Crown treats his exile as a much-much more serious manner. He's accepted by another Sept but it's only because Jacob Morningkill invites him back that he regains his former status. He also kills a number of other Ronin who were willing to die for Arkady because he claimed he could reverse his exiles.<br /> <br /> But yes, I doubt we'll agree on anything which portrays the Ronin as anything other than exiles. Which they can be for any reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-18-2017, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:51:35-07:00","id":1117598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117501#post1117501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such as?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for example, except in Outcast you dont become a Ronin for bullshit reasons.<br /> <br /> Is not a &quot;piss an elder off, a ronin you become&quot; or even maintaining your religion. You really have to screw up to become a Ronin. The former might warrant a loss of renown/a duel to the death but declaring you a Ronin as punishment goes way beyond that.<br /> <br /> Using the example of the Outcast book, a Garou that believes the Veil should be dispose off is not ground enough to declare him a Ronin. He can voice his belief once or twice and depending on how he goes with it he might get beaten up or loose renown. <br /> <br /> It would really take said garou to do try to break the veil in a conscious and deliberate manner to him warrant the Ronin label, which is NOT being Albrecht. He was never a Ronin. Even in his novel he was very much a Silver Fang. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T22:02:20-07:00","id":1117604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117598#post1117598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well for example, except in Outcast you dont become a Ronin for bullshit reasons.<br /> <br /> Is not a &quot;piss an elder off, a ronin you become&quot; or even maintaining your religion. You really have to screw up to become a Ronin. The former might warrant a loss of renown/a duel to the death but declaring you a Ronin as punishment goes way beyond that.<br /> <br /> Using the example of the Outcast book, a Garou that believes the Veil should be dispose off is not ground enough to declare him a Ronin. He can voice his belief once or twice and depending on how he goes with it he might get beaten up or loose renown.<br /> <br /> It would really take said garou to do try to break the veil in a conscious and deliberate manner to him warrant the Ronin label, which is NOT being Albrecht. He was never a Ronin. Even in his novel he was very much a Silver Fang.</div> </div> </div> </div>We never got a sign other than he said he didn't believe in the Veil for his exile.<br /> <br /> Actually, one of the weird things in the books is they don't have many examples of Ronin. There's the Skindancers but we don't have many examples of other Ronin.<br /> <br /> The First Metis doesn't count after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T00:13:48-07:00","id":1117628,"title":"","content":"It will certainly be an interesting 3-4 years of this, I guess.<br /> <br /> Funny thing is, I know people are assuming this game is going to follow the mechanics, lore, etc. of Werewolf to a T.<br /> <br /> First, Redemption, Bloodlines, and all three Hunter the Reckoning games took MANY liberties with the license. I'm positive this will be no different. Certain things simply don't translate well to video game form(nor to fun). I'd argue that Bloodlines was actually better for not following many of the mechanics and rules of VtM. <br /> <br /> This game will also contain some things that might be found in the next iteration of Werewolf(W5), none of which we know about yet(since V5 isn't even close to release). <br /> <br /> As long as Cyanide can capture the heart and soul of the game world, while making it--first and foremost a FUN game, that's what will matter. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T02:09:37-07:00","id":1117646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117577#post1117577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I felt the Garou Nation should make regular use of exile as a way of dealing with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? From the perspective of a TT or LARP game, exile rightfully made a rare option. A dead character means you make a new character. A character stripped of their rank and status can regain them. An exiled character is either a dead character, or a character that is removed from play leaving the player with nothing to do with the rest of the group for however long it takes to reverse their exile.<br /> <br /> In universe the reasoning for ostracism being worse than death to the Garou is discussed very thoroughly. The Garou are so social it's easily ingrained in them that death is better than being shunned. The Bone Gnawers are even stated to get a boost in numbers out of the Garou that are too close to choosing to be Ronin for any other Tribe, but still desperate enough for staying part of the Garou society that they don't want to cross that line, and the Gnawers allow them to stay with an acceptable level of loyalty to at least the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given you CAN join factions (and learn their gifts) I'm inclined to think it won't be the kind of &quot;Ronin&quot; which is treated as a shunned outcast but more a valuable asset that you remain apart of it. </div> </div> </div>We'll have to wait quite a bit I think before we see how this goes exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A &quot;Lone Wolf&quot; versus a outcast and that's the way it should be. Ronin are inherently cool after all. </div> </div> </div>You don't have to play a Ronin to play a lone wolf. I had a character in a larger format game that had three packs die on him over many years of play, and as a higher Rank member of the Sept essentially just did his own thing most of the time and nobody really cared that he wasn't in a permanent pack because even Garou can understand being standoffish at that point. He'd gather up any stragglers from the Cliaths and lead temporary packs on missions and that sort of thing when numbers were needed on top of experience.<br /> <br /> I really don't find anything inherently cool about the Ronin. Probably because they're clearly designed as cautionary tales more than things that are fun to play, but WW could never ignore something that you could technically play getting a book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117594#post1117594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly you treat finding Erebus a different matter than in my games where it's about as easy as finding the Holy Grail and is semi-mythical.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... but that's not how the books describe Erebus at all. Entering and finding redemption isn't exactly easy, but finding Erebus isn't any harder than any other Near Umbra Realm. The Holy Grail is coming out the other side cleansed fully of your sins, not getting to the front gate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Ronin can very often be a person exiled for no damn good reason and who stands for their own beliefs. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Becoming a Ronin requires a Rite (the easy one for those that do it by choice, and the harder one that forces it). As one of the most dire punishments in Garou society, the spirits that empower the rite to make someone a Ronin are going to demand it's for good cause. A Garou can get exiled from a Protectorate and such for no good reason (see Albrecht) but that's not the same as being a Ronin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say, a Garou who refuses to abandon his Homid religion. </div> </div> </div>There's multiple examples of characters (even Camps) that manage to walk the line between human religion and the Garou cult. The basic version is that as long as a Garou upholds the Litany and their duties, there's nothing to punish for believing other stuff too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Garou who needs his pack and tribe is probably understandable but the one who puts what is right above companionship is a figure who deserves respect. </div> </div> </div>Sure, and the one that balances both is even more commended. This is handled in the Renown charts, not an issue of Ronin vs. regular Garou.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T05:09:09-07:00","id":1117677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117151#post1117151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to talk about an ideal WtA game, you would have it set in a rural location. It would be near a state or national park (ideally the map would be 50% public land and 50% private land) and it would include a large town and a dozen or so small towns. A place like Aroostock County in Maine would be ideal, especially since there are a two Native American reservations in the county, so you have a good reason for Wendigo and Uktenu to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see this as a location for a game. Something to keep in mind is that only 5% of the land in the state is publicly owned. Also the largest city in Aroostook Country is Presque Isle at ~9700 people. So if were looking for a bigger urban area the map would have to be expanded to include Bangor (32,500), Augusta (18,700), or Portland (66,600). Augusta and Portland are getting fairly south in the state and some would consider them part of North Massachusetts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T06:02:47-07:00","id":1117692,"title":"","content":"I do not think that you need a big urban area for a sandbox game (Skyrim had around 1,000 characters, the vast majority of whom were generic guards, bandits, etc). You just need a lot of roaming space, and Aroostook County is around 400 times larger than the playable area of Skyrim. Of course, you probably want a car at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T06:17:20-07:00","id":1117696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117604#post1117604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never got a sign other than he said he didn't believe in the Veil for his exile.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said, Outcast aside, how the Ronin are handle by other books. Outcast made it seems that Ronin are declared by the drop of a hat. When that doesnt follow other books or basic logic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117604#post1117604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one of the weird things in the books is they don't have many examples of Ronin. There's the Skindancers but we don't have many examples of other Ronin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That mostly because they suffer from the all decker/no decker at all problem. You cant really, without taking liberties with the setting, run a mix pack of tribe garous and ronins. Either everyone is a Ronin and one is running a pride/shame game. Or one is running a everyones in a tribe game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:42:32-07:00","id":1117726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117692#post1117692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that you need a big urban area for a sandbox game (Skyrim had around 1,000 characters, the vast majority of whom were generic guards, bandits, etc). You just need a lot of roaming space, and Aroostook County is around 400 times larger than the playable area of Skyrim. Of course, you probably want a car at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logging trucks could be wandering monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:50:48-07:00","id":1117774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117692#post1117692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that you need a big urban area for a sandbox game (Skyrim had around 1,000 characters, the vast majority of whom were generic guards, bandits, etc). You just need a lot of roaming space, and Aroostook County is around 400 times larger than the playable area of Skyrim. Of course, you probably want a car at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a video game based there would probably not be 400 times larger than Skyrim's playable area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:08:09-07:00","id":1117856,"title":"","content":"Why not? Daggerfall had an area 4,000 times greater than Skyrim's, and it came out in 1996. I think that they could make a game 1/10th the size of Daggerfall (1/5th with the Penumbra) without any major issues with random character generators, random quest generators, and random monster generators. Random generators are simple nowadays, even with HD graphics, as long as you do not try to do 4K.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:12:06-07:00","id":1117859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117856#post1117856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Daggerfall had an area 4,000 times greater than Skyrim's, and it came out in 1996. I think that they could make a game 1/10th the size of Daggerfall (1/5th with the Penumbra) without any major issues with random character generators, random quest generators, and random monster generators. Random generators are simple nowadays, even with HD graphics, as long as you do not try to do 4K.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because making an overhead map and nearly-identical territory is different from three-dimensional fully voiced areas. For me, I'd prefer they go really well-developed SMALL areas than one huge roaming one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:47:42-07:00","id":1117968,"title":"","content":"The two aren't mutually exclusive. They don't have to go as big as Aya is talking about, but Morrowind (which came out two years before VtMB) had both expansive wilderness areas and well developed towns and so on. It's not some massive technological feat do where sacrificing one must be done to fulfill another considering that it's been done repeatedly in video games for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:59:15-07:00","id":1117977,"title":"","content":"Well, we have some knowledge about the map actually.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dreadcentral.com/news/235724/e3-2017-cyanidewerewolf-apocalypse-seeks-bring-world-darkness-life/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dreadcentral.com/news/23...darkness-life/</a><br /> <br /> <i>I also got to see a working mock-up of Werewolf: The Apocalypse\u2018s map, which you\u2019ll be able to explore in a semi-open fashion. Rather than a true open world, you\u2019ll be able to tackle each zone and resolve its issues in an order of your choosing. Each will be its own instanced area with a border, but that doesn\u2019t mean that what happens in one won\u2019t effect the others. It\u2019s all glued together by a central massive forest hub, where the Garou will roam freely and commune with the spirits. The example Julien gave me of how this communion would work was a hypothetical quest given to you by the spirit of a waterfall. If you do what it wants (say, shut down the coal mine polluting the river), it will let you travel up the waterfall like a super industrious salmon.</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.dreadcentral.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/WereWolf_Artwork_03-1024x525.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <i>Now this is normally the time I\u2019d point to the studio\u2019s pedigree as evidence for how the game might end up, but Cyanide hasn\u2019t really come out with anything like this before. They have done RPGs before with Of Orcs and Men and A Game of Thrones, but neither can compare to what they are trying to do with Werewolf: The Apocalypse. I liked Styx 1 &amp;2, so that gives me confidence. With no release date announced, there\u2019s plenty of time to see how this will shape up. For fans, I think the fact that there\u2019s something in the works from a developer that clearly knows and cares about the property is what matters. So what about you folks? Fans of World of Darkness? Ever try out Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines? What kind of thing are you looking for in your ideal Werewolf: The Apocalypse game? Let me know below!</i><br /> <br /> This really is sounding a lot like V:TM:B and that's not a bad thing. I will say, though, I hope we get some urban areas. I'd like to see a Twin Peaks feel for whatever town exists nearby.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T07:26:16-07:00","id":1118160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117856#post1117856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Daggerfall had an area 4,000 times greater than Skyrim's, and it came out in 1996. I think that they could make a game 1/10th the size of Daggerfall (1/5th with the Penumbra) without any major issues with random character generators, random quest generators, and random monster generators. Random generators are simple nowadays, even with HD graphics, as long as you do not try to do 4K.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daggerfall was a procedurally generated map that used common (within the game) assets to generate dungeons, towns, etc. If you want a game that <i>looks like </i>Daggerfall, then sure, it could be done. It'd not be exactly what you want, though, since the actually unique content wouldn't be all that large.<br /> <br /> Basically, technology is why it can't be done, and why Skyrim is smaller than Daggerfall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1117968#post1117968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two aren't mutually exclusive. They don't have to go as big as Aya is talking about, but Morrowind (which came out two years before VtMB) had both expansive wilderness areas and well developed towns and so on. It's not some massive technological feat do where sacrificing one must be done to fulfill another considering that it's been done repeatedly in video games for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morrowind was smaller than Oblivion and Skyrim, though:<br /> <br /> Skyrim=14.5 sq miles<br /> Oblivion=22 sq miles<br /> Morrowind=9.3 sq miles<br /> <br /> Number crunching here: <a href=\"http://forums.bethsoft.com/topic/1264541-skyrimoblivionmorrowind-heightmap-comparison/\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.bethsoft.com/topic/126...ap-comparison/</a><br /> <br /> To be fair, a lot of Oblivion's map area was behind invisible walls and serving basically as distant terrain you could never reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T09:12:43-07:00","id":1118190,"title":"","content":"And you can just have a few dozen areas where character travel. Shadowrun Returns is set in Seattle, but it does not give access to more than a fraction of the metroplex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T14:12:16-07:00","id":1118274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118160#post1118160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morrowind was smaller than Oblivion and Skyrim, though:<br /> <br /> Skyrim=14.5 sq miles<br /> Oblivion=22 sq miles<br /> Morrowind=9.3 sq miles<br /> <br /> Number crunching here: <a href=\"http://forums.bethsoft.com/topic/1264541-skyrimoblivionmorrowind-heightmap-comparison/\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.bethsoft.com/topic/126...ap-comparison/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Morrowind's smaller yes, that wasn't my point.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm not going to get into the number crunching, those values are considerably off from the lore of the setting. I'm sure there's some concession to game play involved, but Vvardenfell is supposed to be around 250 miles north-to-south. The functional play areas might be considerably smaller (I mean, even if there was no technological hurdle, walking 2500 miles in-play would be tedious beyond belief), but the fictional setting is significantly larger and adequately communicated with the technology of the day. And more importantly, there's a huge amount of detail in the game despite also having a lot of wilderness space; which is the core point. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:11:28-07:00","id":1118316,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute, I don't understand... why would you be Ronin? Why not just have no pack at the beginning? Why not just be a cub? I don't understand why Ronin is a possibility. And does that mean there's no character creation?<br /> <br /> What is the point of the game without a Tribe? Saving Gaia is literally the best part of being Garou. Otherwise, just be a fucking mage or whatever. This makes no sense at all. How are you supposed to get gifts if the spirits don't trust you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2197,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","user":"roleplayrose","date":". 07-19-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:38:09-07:00","id":1118321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118274#post1118274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Morrowind's smaller yes, that wasn't my point.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm not going to get into the number crunching, those values are considerably off from the lore of the setting. I'm sure there's some concession to game play involved, but Vvardenfell is supposed to be around 250 miles north-to-south. The functional play areas might be considerably smaller (I mean, even if there was no technological hurdle, walking 2500 miles in-play would be tedious beyond belief), but the fictional setting is significantly larger and adequately communicated with the technology of the day. And more importantly, there's a huge amount of detail in the game despite also having a lot of wilderness space; which is the core point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is completely relevant because each game represents an area at a significantly smaller scale than they are said to be. Morrowind doesn't communicate in any way that it is 250 miles north to south because it is only 9.3 square miles. That is a considerably smaller area than Daggerfall covered, and not a counterpoint to anything I said. And yes, the numbers are off from the lore in the setting but they are accurate to the actual games.<br /> <br /> I wasn't saying open world couldn't be done, I was saying open world <i>of Daggerfall's scale</i> was unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:14:05-07:00","id":1118330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roleplayrose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118316#post1118316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a minute, I don't understand... why would you be Ronin? Why not just have no pack at the beginning? Why not just be a cub? I don't understand why Ronin is a possibility. And does that mean there's no character creation?<br /> <br /> What is the point of the game without a Tribe? Saving Gaia is literally the best part of being Garou. Otherwise, just be a fucking mage or whatever. This makes no sense at all. How are you supposed to get gifts if the spirits don't trust you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, maybe because when making a sexy intriguing creature of the night you don't want to be a fourteen-year-old adolescent?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ronin are awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, we've already had it stated you can make pacts with Spirits given you can get the &quot;Salmon swimming&quot; Gift. So clearly being a Ronin isn't going to be all that bad (as it should be) and probably more akin to Bloodlines where you're a factionless independent versus some sort of pariah.<br /> <br /> As for fighting for Gaia, I'm hoping it'll be optional with the chance to join Pentex and not have it backfire like joining the Kuei-jin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:26:41-07:00","id":1118334,"title":"","content":"Ronin are not awesome, they are cowards who left the service of Gaia because they just could not hack it. Saying they are awesome is like saying that disserting the military during a time of war is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:27:57-07:00","id":1118335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118334#post1118334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ronin are not awesome, they are cowards who left the service of Gaia because they just could not hack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Ronin is a superior being to all of Gaia's slaves.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:32:20-07:00","id":1118338,"title":"","content":"Ronin are inferior beings. They lack Rank, Renown, and Tribe, so they will never be allowed to breed with Kinfolk. They are looked down upon by the Spirits themselves and are always at risk of falling to the Wyrm. Most of them will die in a gutter if they do not end up walking the spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:44:54-07:00","id":1118341,"title":"","content":"So Ronin are basically pariahs who are considered okay to be tormented and abused in the moral absolutism of the game's setting?<br /> <br /> But if they're making them protagonists of the game... maybe the moral absolutism isn't severe as it is, or the game's developers are taking an alternate interpretation of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:01:08-07:00","id":1118344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118321#post1118321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it is completely relevant because each game represents an area at a significantly smaller scale than they are said to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does that have do to with the idea that the game can't use an open-world setup that captures both a decently sized wilderness and human population centers, and lack detail?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morrowind doesn't communicate in any way that it is 250 miles north to south because it is only 9.3 square miles. </div> </div> </div>Well, the game isn't any square miles. That figure assumes a specific scale of map units to real world measurements, which the thread doesn't really thoroughly justify to anything I can find (like, there's a statement of what that scale is, but never why it should be accepted as accurate). Given the exponential effect, it doesn't take much of an increase in that scale to end up with a much larger playable area equivalent to the real world.<br /> <br /> As well, multiple threads about that (including that thread) have people expressing to the agreement of others that Morrowind feels bigger than the later TES games because of how well it uses the smaller map to communicate the perception of distance without needing actual digital distance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is a considerably smaller area than Daggerfall covered, and not a counterpoint to anything I said. </div> </div> </div>And... nothing you said was much of a counterpoint to what I was saying... so... yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wasn't saying open world couldn't be done, I was saying open world <i>of Daggerfall's scale</i> was unlikely. </div> </div> </div>So... were are you going with this then? Because it seems like you're trying to argue as if I'm in lockstep with Aya, even when I'm not.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a><br /> <br /> You're being baited, just ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:01:59-07:00","id":1118345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118330#post1118330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, maybe because when making a sexy intriguing creature of the night you don't want to be a fourteen-year-old adolescent?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ronin are awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, we've already had it stated you can make pacts with Spirits given you can get the &quot;Salmon swimming&quot; Gift. So clearly being a Ronin isn't going to be all that bad (as it should be) and probably more akin to Bloodlines where you're a factionless independent versus some sort of pariah.<br /> <br /> As for fighting for Gaia, I'm hoping it'll be optional with the chance to join Pentex and not have it backfire like joining the Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to be a &quot;Creature of the Night\u00a8 then be a fucking vampire. (Or Demon or Wraith or whatever) That's not what Garou are, nor is it what they should be. <br /> <br /> Ronin are not awesome. Ronin are shitheads who left Gaia's service because they are selfish, or stupid, or evil. If the planet itself is crying for help and you say no thanks, you are a moron and deserve to be eaten for your trouble. <br /> <br /> And you shouldn't be a &quot;factionless independent&quot; as a Ronin, you should have the Rite of Gaia's Vengeful Teeth brought upon you and every step should be painful until you sacrifice yourself for the greater good. <br /> <br /> I guess this just saves me money, but it's really sad that a game that deserves a good treatment and a good story is going to do something so marginally related to the actual point of the game and silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:11:15-07:00","id":1118347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roleplayrose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118345#post1118345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be a &quot;Creature of the Night\u00a8 then be a fucking vampire. (Or Demon or Wraith or whatever) That's not what Garou are, nor is it what they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Garou are night creatures in that they are tied to Luna instead of Helios. But that is a whole different bag apart from Vampire's assumptions, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:13:55-07:00","id":1118348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118341#post1118341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ronin are basically pariahs who are considered okay to be tormented and abused in the moral absolutism of the game's setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm no. Ronin are pariahs who are shunned as punishment and despised by the spirits that the Ronin let down by not stepping up to their duties. Tormenting and abusing them directly isn't actually acceptable by the general rules of Garou society.<br /> <br /> The torment and abuse comes from the perception that Ronin frequently fall to service to the Wyrm. The Wyrm's forces offer companionship and paths to respect and power that Ronin are cut of from otherwise. The Ronin are stuck with either suffering the misery their condition implies, or being assumed to be traitors if they manage to find a place outside of that misery. And unlike many real world comparison the Garou Nation approaches a level of reasonable risk assessment in that assumption.<br /> <br /> There are Garou that question this (particularly the Children of Gaia) because the absolute shunning producing Wyrm servants isn't a good outcome, and would advocate a more tempered shunning or just not forcing Ronin status a punishment at all. Garou, unlike spirits, are not compelled to specific actions by their fundamental natures, and can examine the situation and change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if they're making them protagonists of the game... maybe the moral absolutism isn't severe as it is, or the game's developers are taking an alternate interpretation of the setting. </div> </div> </div>The second one is the most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:24:54-07:00","id":1118351,"title":"","content":"Edit: Actually, nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-19-2017, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:28:20-07:00","id":1118354,"title":"","content":"Bluntly, I think Outcasts is the best treatment of Ronin and portrayed them far more interestingly than the shitty portrayal in canon books. I also consider it canon and it seems the game is going for that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:31:33-07:00","id":1118355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118338#post1118338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ronin are inferior beings. They lack Rank, Renown, and Tribe, so they will never be allowed to breed with Kinfolk. They are looked down upon by the Spirits themselves and are always at risk of falling to the Wyrm. Most of them will die in a gutter if they do not end up walking the spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was joking (somewhat) but what the hell does reknown have to do with anything? It's a meaningless system which the accumulation of just shows the Garou cares more about the points of. As for spirits, the spirits which shun them are clearly not all of them or even most of them as the Skindancers have Minotaur and now Tick angling to become the head of their tribe. As for the risk of falling to the Wyrm, so does all Garou.<br /> <br /> But I suspect we're running into a wall because I consider the Garou Nation to be corrupt and failing and not worth anyone actually caring about.<br /> <br /> Then again, I've always run a very dark and cynical Werewolf game. Ronin are very useful in games where its clear the GN is a sinking ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:32:32-07:00","id":1118356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118348#post1118348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm no. Ronin are pariahs who are shunned as punishment and despised by the spirits that the Ronin let down by not stepping up to their duties. Tormenting and abusing them directly isn't actually acceptable by the general rules of Garou society.<br /> <br /> The torment and abuse comes from the perception that Ronin frequently fall to service to the Wyrm. The Wyrm's forces offer companionship and paths to respect and power that Ronin are cut of from otherwise. The Ronin are stuck with either suffering the misery their condition implies, or being assumed to be traitors if they manage to find a place outside of that misery. And unlike many real world comparison the Garou Nation approaches a level of reasonable risk assessment in that assumption.<br /> <br /> There are Garou that question this (particularly the Children of Gaia) because the absolute shunning producing Wyrm servants isn't a good outcome, and would advocate a more tempered shunning or just not forcing Ronin status a punishment at all. Garou, unlike spirits, are not compelled to specific actions by their fundamental natures, and can examine the situation and change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like what the game's setting itself is saying is much more reasonable than the &quot;Gaia is the Ultimate Good and all who refuse to fight for Gaia are irredeemable&quot; mantra that some people are saying, with the latter being a caricature of the former. Sounds fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:33:52-07:00","id":1118358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118347#post1118347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Garou are night creatures in that they are tied to Luna instead of Helios. But that is a whole different bag apart from Vampire's assumptions, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that you have a point, but they are usually referred to as Children of Luna or Gaia, not &quot;Of the Night&quot; because that has heavy connotations, especially in pop culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:34:10-07:00","id":1118359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1118356#post1118356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like what the game's setting itself is saying is much more reasonable than the &quot;Gaia is the Ultimate Good and all who refuse to fight for Gaia are irredeemable&quot; mantra that some people are saying, with the latter being a caricature of the former. Sounds fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not like we're not actually going to be fighting for Gaia.<br /> <br /> We're getting gifts from 