2906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T04:02:55-07:00","id":1140480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140282#post1140282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> redeemed ronin is not a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the idea of a ronin that can be redeemed or fall entirely to the wyrm depending on decisions, great idea for game story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:02:27-07:00","id":1140517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140422#post1140422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, but they don't loose rank benefits. Usually ronin is not amnesiac so he will still have gifts of his former rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's pretty much the only thing they'll retain. All the other actual rank benefits will be lost, because they no longer have rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T09:17:06-07:00","id":1140533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140480#post1140480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like the idea of a ronin that can be redeemed or fall entirely to the wyrm depending on decisions, great idea for game story.</div> </div> </div> </div>But remember that path to redeem Ronin is not an easy one. First of all: why the character is Ronin?<br /> 1. He/she offended tribe/Gaia/sept/caern<br /> 2. Someone doesn't like him/her (similar to Lord Albrecht story)<br /> 3. He/she chose solitude.<br /> Now most of the tribes will not try to find out why he/she is a Ronin. They will propably simply assume that he/she is a criminal. So joining the tribe won't be easy: <br /> 1. Children of Gaia - the most tolerant and trusting (to the point of naivete) tribe. They will propably accept Ronin unconditionally<br /> 2. Bone Gnawers - they are treated poorly by the rest of Garou Nation so who cares. Unconditionally.<br /> 3. Glass Walkers - only if you have resources/skills that can be useful for the tribe.<br /> 4. Get of Fenris - you have to kick some asses to earn their respect.<br /> 5. Shadow Lords - if you are good enough to fit their standards you're in. They don't like to waste worthy people.<br /> 6. Uktena - you have to be a Native American or have some knowledge/know some secrets to interest them<br /> And now the hard part<br /> 7. Black Furies - you have to be a woman.<br /> 8. Red Talons - you have to be lupus<br /> 9. Silver Fangs - you have to be pure blooded<br /> 10. Wendigo - you have to be Native American<br /> 11. Fianna - you have to be from Celtic descent or be able to drink enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> 12. Silent Striders - as they are the messengers for Garou Nation they won't propably trust any Ronin. Maybe if he/she can keep up their pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:13:11-07:00","id":1140539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140479#post1140479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the impression that it will have similarities, but it will be a different game with a completely different mood, way more dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant similar in the sense of being a sort of a sandbox (I don't know how else to call it) game - with different locations you can travel to, different and meaningful ways of tackling challenges, real consequences to your decisions, rewards for completing tasks in a better way, various sides to join and/or support, resources management, development of the character's capabilities. I think and feel that <i>Bloodlines</i> really did all those elements in a very good way - or at least they tried, and in the case of those less successful elements even if the meat and/or details weren't properly developed, what is there still enhances the game's mood at the very least. The final result is much better than <i>Knights of the Old Republic 1 </i>and <i>2</i>, I'd say.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to the upcoming W:tA game being 'way more dark' - <i>Vampire: </i><i><i>The Masquerade Bloodlines</i> </i>starts with you Sire being killed publicly, the game camera showing different Kindred as they watch coolly. The game has drinking human blood as an integral part of it, to the point when you have to press space within a few seconds so your character doesn't drain someone to death. You interact with other Kindred living amidst the humanity, the humans completely unaware due to the Masquerade.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><u><b>Major spoilers for Vampire: <i>The Masquerade Bloodlines</i></b></u></i></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> There is a Tzimisce Vicissitude monsters snuff film. A Nagaraja spooking, killing and eating a 'supernatural-busting' TV show crew. A Malkavian whose dual personality -related issues can result in one of the personalities 'dying' ; and another Malkavian who is terrifying enough merely through his recorded musings. Your Ghoul kidnaps a human for you to feed from. Interactions with other Nightfolk - the Kuei-Jin, a Garou, Asian Technocrat True Mage(s) - are hostile. The Kindred 'authorities' are often clueless about what is going on, and send you out into the night. The mythology of the Kindred (Lilith, Caine) is also present; as is the Jyhad. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know that Wt:A has the Wyrm and other aspects that can be considered and called dark, but can you really get substantially more dark - rather than a different kind of dark - than V:tM, and <i><i>Bloodlines</i></i><i>? </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140480#post1140480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like the idea of a ronin that can be redeemed or fall entirely to the wyrm depending on decisions, great idea for game story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there should definitely be a Wyrm-related option/pathway for the character. Perhaps a 'morality meter' (Gaia / Wyrm meter) that goes through the whole game, and maybe a chance to dance the Black Spiral at some point - perhaps only if the character earns it through continuous actions throughout the game.<br /> <br /> And in an expansion perhaps a Weaver-related option/path could be added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-15-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:46:09-07:00","id":1140578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140539#post1140539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the upcoming W:tA game being 'way more dark'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup Bloodlines was a very good game that I would easily play even now.<br /> <br /> But the new Werewolf game will use more advanced stuff as a more modern version of the classic WoD, the game will come out while White-Wolf already makes plans for W5. So newer development equals more advaanced ideas, better programming tools etc.etc.<br /> <br /> IMHO all WoD games are dark, its just that werewolf can be far more brutal dark, or savage dark, adding more metaphysically dark elements of the umbral environments, or places that only Garou dare to tread. Yeah we are all monsters and the vampire game had great dark mood, but if it came out nowadays it would have even greater atmosphere. But werewolf even then is far more alien IMHO and that can make it go even deeper to darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T12:22:20-07:00","id":1140591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140533#post1140533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But remember that path to redeem Ronin is not an easy one. First of all: why the character is Ronin?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Thats why they make this choice of a character, because it can cover an entire campaign to finally redeem a ronin, or half a campaign and the other half to reveal the higher reason pf his redemption. The ronin idea is one that may change with further development of the game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140533#post1140533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now most of the tribes will not try to find out why he/she is a Ronin. They will propably simply assume that he/she is a criminal. So joining the tribe won't be easy:<br /> 1. Children of Gaia - the most tolerant and trusting (to the point of naivete) tribe. They will propably accept Ronin unconditionally<br /> 2. Bone Gnawers - they are treated poorly by the rest of Garou Nation so who cares. Unconditionally.<br /> 3. Glass Walkers - only if you have resources/skills that can be useful for the tribe.<br /> 4. Get of Fenris - you have to kick some asses to earn their respect.<br /> 5. Shadow Lords - if you are good enough to fit their standards you're in. They don't like to waste worthy people.<br /> 6. Uktena - you have to be a Native American or have some knowledge/know some secrets to interest them<br /> And now the hard part<br /> 7. Black Furies - you have to be a woman.<br /> 8. Red Talons - you have to be lupus<br /> 9. Silver Fangs - you have to be pure blooded<br /> 10. Wendigo - you have to be Native American<br /> 11. Fianna - you have to be from Celtic descent or be able to drink enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> 12. Silent Striders - as they are the messengers for Garou Nation they won't propably trust any Ronin. Maybe if he/she can keep up their pace.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.Not exactly the Children of Gaia are not as soft hearted as you think. A wolf always tests the members of his pack, in the rough way of testing.<br /> 2. The gnawers are tricky and cunning and will follow the same rough testing principle like the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Children of Gaia, they may be the omegas of the Garou nation but they are still alphas in their territorries and woe to the unwise who will no respect their rule. (I had a Silver Fang player that disrespected a Gnawer Elder and he was ritually butt-spanked).<br /> 3.Not only, unfortuately the Walkers will do test you against the Wyrm and probably if you can use the weaver at your advantage while fighting the Wyrm.<br /> 4.Yes kick some bottoms in a suicidal way probably, they also value high discipline, probably even aiding them to raid another Garou sept.<br /> 5.You are unworthy no matter what you do, in order to enter the Lords you need to do something extreme, like killing a shadowlord of the sept while benefitting the Shadowlords sept with that action in a major way. That would impress them.<br /> 6.Yup native American and recover tribal sacred property long lost to the wyrm or the wyrm bringer tribes.<br /> 7.Or a Metis, man how much I crave for the option of a metis character.<br /> 8.Lupus and benefit the tribe in human skulls.<br /> 9.And silver haired <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Kidding, the Fangs demand personal sacrifice or absolute proven loyalty appart from the pure breeding, the hard way.<br /> 10. And kill a bunch of Fenrir or Fangs maybe. Man I love Garou conflict.<br /> 11.And hang out with fairies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 12.Striders might accept a ronin if he aided them in a rescue mission and yup if he is fast and stealthy.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:15:12-07:00","id":1140612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1117007-cyanide-s-werewolf-the-apocalypse-video-game?p=1140591#post1140591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.Not exactly the Children of Gaia are not as soft hearted as you think. A wolf always tests the members of his pack, in the rough way of testing.<br /> 2. The gnawers are tricky and cunning and will follow the same rough testing principle like the Children of Gaia, they may be the omegas of the Garou nation but they are still alphas in their territorries and woe to the unwise who will no respect their rule. (I had a Silver Fang player that disrespected a Gnawer Elder and he was ritually butt-spanked).<br /> 3.Not only, unfortuately the Walkers will do test you against the Wyrm and probably if you can use the weaver at your advantage while fighting the Wyrm.<br /> 4.Yes kick some bottoms in a suicidal way probably, they also value high discipline, probably even aiding them to raid another Garou sept.<br /> 5.You are unworthy no matter what you do, in order to enter the Lords you need to do something extreme, like killing a shadowlord of the sept while benefitting the Shadowlords sept with that action in a major way. That would impress them.<br /> 6.Yup native American and recover tribal sacred property long lost to the wyrm or the wyrm bringer tribes.<br /> 7.Or a Metis, man how much I crave for the option of a metis character.<br /> 8.Lupus and benefit the tribe in human skulls.<br /> 9.And silver haired <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Kidding, the Fangs demand personal sacrifice or absolute proven loyalty appart from the pure breeding, the hard way.<br /> 10. And kill a bunch of Fenrir or Fangs maybe. Man I love Garou conflict.<br /> 11.And hang out with fairies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 12.Striders might accept a ronin if he aided them in a rescue mission and yup if he is fast and stealthy.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I presented here simplified version. I tried to put these tribes in order from the easiest way to bring the Ronin back to Garou Nation to the hardest. And I'm still not convinced that making Ronin the main character is a good choice. I would rather see the campaign the way they did in most D&amp;D based video games, with auspices and tribes working as character classes. And to be a leader of the pack of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> As for conflicts between tribes I am sure that you would appreciate the way that my friend's Shadow Lord resolve that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:15:12-07:00","id":1140613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally p